      },
      "message": "Use floating-point aspect ratio for thermal camera range (#3998)\n\n* Use floating-point aspect ratio for thermal camera range\n\nImageWidth() and ImageHeight() are integers, so the division truncated\nbefore the result reached the double. A 320x240 camera was treated as\naspect 1 instead of 1.3333, and a portrait image truncated to 0, which\nthen divides into the vertical FOV and yields an infinite range.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Opus 5\nSigned-off-by: Puja <catplotlib@gmail.com>\n\n* Cast both operands explicitly\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Opus 5\nSigned-off-by: Puja <catplotlib@gmail.com>",
